da501c5a7ed","alt":"Six sheep compared with four goats"},{"key":"c-selector-week-4","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/icons-v2/week-4.png","sha256":"676d9f71e8992eedf68235b44224fb63184a99e7dca15c5c95f30d7973173213","alt":"Four ducks and three cheetahs"},{"key":"c-selector-literacy","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/icons-v1/literacy.png","sha256":"ca49dfc7da831494724823618a65ad2f1c1c66b1c267503fe9413ac7f9403bfe","alt":"Gerry exploring animal words and counting"},{"key":"c-selector-reading","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/icons-v1/reading.png","sha256":"11f9d32b1b1b6047c9639a6bf1e3551c5547f733d3a98ed53fd194ca628a20fd","alt":"Penny reading an animal picture book"},{"key":"c-selector-phonics","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/icons-v1/phonics.png","sha256":"30918a6201784d0c0055ec3d2670fd3ee62fd326ae1b7c8581f1b12c8dd5c1d9","alt":"Don listening to animal words"},{"key":"c-selector-games","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/icons-v1/games.png","sha256":"c04fac283160128e5cdd5f66bf11443863709d1f3741bea99345b0c4a91257b8","alt":"Wanda playing an animal-picture puzzle"},{"key":"c1-speech-uniform-01","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/speech/week1-uniform-v1/01-mole-digging.png","sha256":"ac33f528b80d369b8f3f6573db3e66b1434206b4b8d2c79317953d474897626d","alt":"One clearly recognizable whole mole actively digging in soil with visible holes. Show the animal and its action together; no additional moles.","width":1448,"height":1086},{"key":"c1-speech-uniform-02","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/speech/week1-uniform-v1/02-two-moles.png","sha256":"45896ea195eeb1efa7b14c1eb599b9b895736a4a240b527f0e5eed97843f4e3c","alt":"Exactly two complete, easy-to-count moles, well spaced on a simple game-board/soil base. No four-mole comparison group in this picture.","width":1448,"height":1086},{"key":"c1-speech-uniform-03","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/speech/week1-uniform-v1/03-four-moles.png","sha256":"82db419b6c6e209d6374485aa79ae9efe36a3751611ec876141d8576e2606b8b","alt":"Exactly four complete moles, evenly spaced, matching the two-mole card's animal size and visual style.","width":1448,"height":1086},{"key":"c1-speech-uniform-04","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/speech/week1-uniform-v1/04-compare-moles.png","sha256":"c520878f15f4185d5a48508d02c9a755d49aac499ce5cdf6ad4e461bd3de26dc","alt":"Two clearly separated groups: exactly two moles on the left and four on the right. Same animal size/spacing; draw attention to the four-mole group while explaining greater than. Do not mix all six into one group.","width":1448,"height":1086},{"key":"c1-speech-uniform-05","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/speech/week1-uniform-v1/05-two-hedgehogs.png","sha256":"b82a2601eb917d5bbf0be93536c2ffb1ca80afa02e4a4930d75173d9dfd1e565","alt":"Exactly two whole hedgehogs together, with clear space around each animal. This is the baseline count before adding one.","width":1448,"height":1086},{"key":"c1-speech-uniform-06","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/speech/week1-uniform-v1/06-one-more.png","sha256":"83e007c0fad2c97f7c6b2f44ab15f20db5bb36a8cbb6922544910c4b310ea05d","alt":"A clear two-to-three sequence: two hedgehogs first, then one new hedgehog joins, ending with exactly three together. For still art use clearly separated before/after panels with a joining arrow; never use unexplained ghost copies.","width":1448,"height":1086},{"key":"c1-speech-uniform-07","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/speech/week1-uniform-v1/07-five-hedgehogs.png","sha256":"68e8bf6814bfe2487b92fac098e08668f6808562798f909cdd02d8e1dee9fe38","alt":"Exactly five whole hedgehogs, all still together. Use a readily countable two-and-three arrangement. Do not show a departing animal yet.","width":1448,"height":1086},{"key":"c1-speech-uniform-08","path":"apps/assets/month10/level-c/speech/week1-uniform-v1/08-one-less.png","sha256":"d50db36a2b9352d3dba6be14919b616a1fa8673b65ec488e685c5a519f015215","alt":"A clear five-to-four sequence: start with five, show one leaving, end with exactly f